                                        "entry_id": "6d3e0c70-ee2b-3da5-9e6c-bdd2a75d021b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make beer by steeping a starch source in water and fermenting the resulting sweet liquid with yeast."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4e6fd2d5-8430-3842-a1b8-b83bd80262a5",
                                        "entry_id": "6d3e0c70-ee2b-3da5-9e6c-bdd2a75d021b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To foment or prepare, as by brewing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "67b676de-5792-410b-af5d-092df8bb760f",
                                                "sense_id": "4e6fd2d5-8430-3842-a1b8-b83bd80262a5",
                                                "text": "Hence with thy brew’d inchantments, foul deceiver […]",
                                                "translation": "Comus",
                                                "english": "Comus"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9760381d-3a51-36b1-bb43-5d78418df80b",
                                        "entry_id": "6d3e0c70-ee2b-3da5-9e6c-bdd2a75d021b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To attend to the business, or go through the processes, of brewing or making beer."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "47c43340-593f-41c0-8ea5-19a3789cc8d7",
                                                "sense_id": "9760381d-3a51-36b1-bb43-5d78418df80b",
                                                "text": "I wash, wring, brew, bake, scour, dress meat and drink […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9f6486c3-ac07-3dd5-9f3d-12a29a1da7e0",
                                        "entry_id": "6d3e0c70-ee2b-3da5-9e6c-bdd2a75d021b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To be in a state of preparation; to be mixing, forming, or gathering."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "08cb91bf-70e8-414a-a46a-98e45448e0d2",
                                                "sense_id": "9f6486c3-ac07-3dd5-9f3d-12a29a1da7e0",
                                                "text": "There is some ill a-brewing towards my rest,"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9187cb44-cb42-4379-a3d9-89c3be1c90bd",
                                                "sense_id": "9f6486c3-ac07-3dd5-9f3d-12a29a1da7e0",
                                                "text": "Of course, no one knows what kind of flu season is brewing, the perfect storm of a new strain hitting a largely unvaccinated population or a mercifully mild few months."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ad8d7cf-ae90-4822-95b1-ae98ba034282",
                                                "sense_id": "9f6486c3-ac07-3dd5-9f3d-12a29a1da7e0",
                                                "text": "Grant may have considered that only a performance of the very highest quality could keep him in a job - and the way his players started the game gave the 55-year-old shelter from the storm that was brewing."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4c555d61-bd7a-3d59-9bee-e84264cdb041",
                                        "entry_id": "6d3e0c70-ee2b-3da5-9e6c-bdd2a75d021b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To boil or seethe; to cook."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "beac948e-3526-4066-9d8e-7f171c173463",
                                                "sense_id": "4c555d61-bd7a-3d59-9bee-e84264cdb041",
                                                "text": "She had one day to get up very early in the morning to brew, when the other servants said to her: 'You had better mind you don't get up too early, and you mustn't put any fire under the copper before two o'clock.'"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "brew",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "324354ae-7368-3ccf-addd-7d0997b77f03",
                                        "entry_id": "4aa2585d-91ac-3674-9a5d-e492a5e5d4bd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The mixture formed by brewing; that which is brewed; a brewage, such as tea or beer."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b3564e28-8078-4de5-9a08-b22c504a6d2d",
                                                "sense_id": "324354ae-7368-3ccf-addd-7d0997b77f03",
                                                "text": "Six great bottles of one of the Hong Kong brews had been brought to wash down the brandy and the fragments of rice and mee and meat-fibres that clung to the back teeth."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a792b691-f869-3529-bb41-b5724ffe44f3",
                                        "entry_id": "4aa2585d-91ac-3674-9a5d-e492a5e5d4bd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The mixture formed by brewing; that which is brewed; a brewage, such as tea or beer.",
                                            "A serving of beer."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9bf084e4-bd96-4a4b-8673-9ec777566e21",
                                                "sense_id": "a792b691-f869-3529-bb41-b5724ffe44f3",
                                                "text": "Player, give me some brew and I might just chill / But I'm the type that like to light another joint like Cypress Hill"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d8c66f23-843f-3f06-83a8-dec0668daf64",
                                        "entry_id": "4aa2585d-91ac-3674-9a5d-e492a5e5d4bd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The mixture formed by brewing; that which is brewed; a brewage, such as tea or beer.",
                                            "A cup of tea."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "British",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f31bb89a-9104-439b-9b98-f5d6031241b5",
                                                "sense_id": "d8c66f23-843f-3f06-83a8-dec0668daf64",
                                                "text": "Landlady: You're not stoppin' for a brew?\nGene Hunt: No thanks, love. Better crack on."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "438cf4ff-56f5-3891-8271-d087c4280d2d",
                                        "entry_id": "4aa2585d-91ac-3674-9a5d-e492a5e5d4bd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A boiled concoction or mixture of liquids and other ingredients."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ed8b548-7783-4223-adc0-0e4fc6f18c6e",
                                                "sense_id": "438cf4ff-56f5-3891-8271-d087c4280d2d",
                                                "text": "In the Middle Ages, when witchcraft and thaumaturgic practices were rampant over Europe, sorceresses did a roaring trade in magic brews designed to excite the passion or to preserve affection."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
